For a categorical variable with k levels affecting occupancy and the null model for detection, there should be k-1 effects on occupancy (which represent a difference in occupancy from the reference level) + 1 intercept for occupancy (representing the reference level) + 1 intercept for detection.  So the df output looks like it's counting the parameters correctly.  I don't know enough about dredge to know why it only shows a + instead of displaying all the k-1 effects of the categorical variables.  If you post the model summary for occu(~1 ~bvg_rmn,data=umf) we could see if the results make sense.

