The reason bvg class 1 isn't included is because it's the intercept.  With k levels, you will have k-1 effects plus the intercept.  However there seems to be a serious estimation problem, based on these results.  I'm guessing the levels of bvg_remnan categories add to 100%, or nearly 100%.  If that's the case then the categories are completely collinear, and you can't use all the levels in the model.  You might just include 1 or 2 of the veg types that you have a theoretical reason to believe have a strong influence on occupancy.

